ability, responsibility, problem solving, but hot temper and know-it-all may affect crew cooperation. No direct crew cooperation evidence either. Both have similar crew concerns.\n\nCandidate A: strong anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership, but show-off, not open to new ideas. No info on stress, reliability, etc. Candidate C: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, understands tech, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nGiven the criteria, B seems strongest overall, despite concerns. D also strong but temper may be more severe. I'd likely keep B as provisional recommendation, but ask for more info on A and C. However we need to make a contribution that moves discussion forward, maybe bring up candidate A's strengths and concerns, compare to B.\n\nThus: I will say I still recommend B, but note that A's ability to anticipate dangerous situations and see complex connections could be valuable, yet his show-off attitude and resistance to new ideas raise crew cooperation concerns, making him less suitable than B. Also note C's quick decision making and calmness are good, but communication issues and egocentric attitude are problematic.\n\nThus my vote remains B.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
